  "body": "### What is the issue with the HTML Standard?\n\nThe interception state is first set [unconditionally](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#commit-a-navigate-event:~:text=Set%20event%27s%20interception%20state%20to%20%22committed%22%2E), then afterwards its value is [used in an if condition](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#commit-a-navigate-event:~:text=If%20event%27s%20interception%20state%20is%20not%20%22none%22%3A,-Switch).\n\nIIUC, based on the pre-precommit-handler implementation in Gecko and the tests the interception state should be set inside [inside the if](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#commit-a-navigate-event:~:text=If%20event%27s%20interception%20state%20is%20not%20%22none%22%3A,-Switch).\n\ncc @noamr @zcorpan ",
